Here is the commit message:
ACCUMULO-4349 Fix test bind logic to pass regardless of
 network configuration

ServerSocket will bind to all interfaces which can cause the test to fail
when it expects that subsequent attempts to bind the same port will fail.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the `ServerSocket` binding to all available network interfaces, which led to failures in tests that expected subsequent binding attempts on the same port to fail. This behavior could vary depending on the network configuration, resulting in inconsistent test outcomes.

Here is the patch:

   @Test(expected = UnknownHostException.class)
   public void testStartServerUsedPort() throws Exception {
     int port = getFreePort(1024);
+    InetAddress addr = InetAddress.getByName("localhost");
     // Bind to the port
-    ServerSocket s = new ServerSocket(port);
+    ServerSocket s = new ServerSocket(port, 50, addr);
     ((ConfigurationCopy) factory.getConfiguration()).set(Property.TSERV_CLIENTPORT, Integer.toString(port));
     try {
       startServer();
     } finally {
       s.close();
     }
   }

